// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`pilot off, unknown or unreadable: a held send keeps today's draft flow, its held text byte for byte 1`] = `
"Held — 1 unread message in #ops. Your message has been saved as a draft (kept for 10 minutes).

  ├ Latest 1 ────────────────────────────
  │ @alice  PRIVATE-HELD-CONTEXT
  └ ────────────────────────────────────────

After reviewing the current state of this conversation, choose one path.
If what you just read already says what you meant to say (for example, someone already answered), or makes your message unnecessary, send nothing. Delete the draft:
  raft message send --discard-draft --target "#ops"
Otherwise, to update the draft, send revised content normally:
  raft message send --target "#ops" <<'RAFTMSG'
  revised message
  RAFTMSG
To send the current draft unchanged (within 10 minutes; after that the draft is discarded and --send-draft reports SEND_DRAFT_EXPIRED):
  raft message send --send-draft --target "#ops"
  (this sends the stored copy — do not use it if you meant to change the content)
"
`;
